   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div></div><div></div><div></div><div style=\"font-size:13px;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,arial,freesans,clean,sans-serif;color:rgb(34,34,34);border:none;line-height:20px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><p style=\"margin:1em 0px\"><strong><em>[To those on this list in the social sciences and humanities: Please forward this announcement to your grad group/departmental listservs or other groups that may be interested in qualitative text analysis.]</em></strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Hi all,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">This Friday at the <a href=\"http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,238);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.noamross.net/davis-r-users-group.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468164108000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0kfIMMSfMhwXBb32iA59ov\">Davis R Users Group</a>, Mallory Johnson will give a presentation on doing qualitative text analysis in R using RDQA.  From Mallory:</p>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin:1em 0px;border-left-width:4px;border-left-style:solid;border-left-color:rgb(221,221,221);padding:0px 1em;color:rgb(119,119,119);quotes:none\">\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">R is most often associated with quantitative analysis, but the platform is also useful for qualitative research.  Friday’s presentation will introduce the R package for Qualitative Data Analysis (RQDA), a qualitative analysis software that resides within the frame of R.  RQDA’s simple to use GUI makes organizing and analyzing textual data easy.  Use it for organizing field notes, theory building, or even literature reviews— any time you need to search for keywords, themes, or references across multiple text files. </p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Per usual, the presentation + Q&amp;A will run from 10-11 in Wickson 2124, and we will have open co-work time from 11-12.   Webcast info to come, and materials from the talk will be available on the blog afterwards.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Best,</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1em 0px\">Noam Ross<br>Graduate Group in Ecology<br>Department of Environmental Science and Policy<br>University of California at Davis<br><a href=\"http://www.noamross.net/\" style=\"color:rgb(51,51,238);text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.noamross.net/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792468164108000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1L2gLKxZ5BVRWiBAWHD38w\">http://www.noamross.net/</a><br>twitter: @noamross</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdj4qKipbVG8gdGhvc2Ugb24gdGhpcyBsaXN0IGluIHRoZSBzb2NpYWwgc2NpZW5jZXMgYW5k\r\nIGh1bWFuaXRpZXMsIHBsZWFzZSBmb3J3YXJkIHRoaXMgYW5ub3VuY2VtZW50IHRvIHlvdXIgZ3Jh\r\nZCBncm91cC9kZXBhcnRtZW50YWwgbGlzdHNlcnZzXSoqKjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2Pkhp\r\nIGFsbCw8ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rpdj48ZGl2PlRoaXMgRnJpZGF5IGF0IHRoZSBbRGF2aXMgUiBVc2Vy\r\ncyBHcm91cF0oaHR0cDovL3d3dy5ub2Ftcm9zcy5uZXQvZGF2aXMtci11c2Vycy1ncm91cC5odG1s\r\nKSwgTWFsbG9yeSBKb2huc29uIHdpbGwgZ2l2ZSBhIHByZXNlbnRhdGlvbiBvbiBkb2luZyBxdWFs\r\naXRhdGl2ZSB0ZXh0IGFuYWx5c2lzIGluIFIgdXNpbmcgUkRRQS4gJm5ic3A7RnJvbSBNYWxsb3J5\r\nOjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+Jmd0OyZuYnNwOzxzcGFuIHN0eWxlPSJmb250LXNp\r\nemU6IDEzLjE5OTk5OTgwOTI2NTFweDsgbGluZS1oZWlnaHQ6IDE5Ljc5OTk5OTIzNzA2MDVweDsi\r\nPlIgaXMgbW9zdCBvZnRlbiBhc3NvY2lhdGVkIHdpdGggcXVhbnRpdGF0aXZlIGFuYWx5c2lzLCBi\r\ndXQgdGhlIHBsYXRmb3JtIGlzIGFsc28gdXNlZnVsIGZvciBxdWFsaXRhdGl2ZSByZXNlYXJjaC4m\r\nbmJzcDsgRnJpZGF5J3MgcHJlc2VudGF0aW9uIHdpbGwgaW50cm9kdWNlIHRoZSBSIHBhY2thZ2Ug\r\nZm9yIFF1YWxpdGF0aXZlIERhdGEgQW5hbHlzaXMgKFJRREEpLCBhIHF1YWxpdGF0aXZlIGFuYWx5\r\nc2lzIHNvZnR3YXJlIHRoYXQgcmVzaWRlcyB3aXRoaW4gdGhlIGZyYW1lIG9mIFIuJm5ic3A7IFJR\r\nREEncyBzaW1wbGUgdG8gdXNlIEdVSSBtYWtlcyBvcmdhbml6aW5nIGFuZCBhbmFseXppbmcgdGV4\r\ndHVhbCBkYXRhIGVhc3kuJm5ic3A7IFVzZSBpdCBmb3Igb3JnYW5pemluZyBmaWVsZCBub3Rlcywg\r\ndGhlb3J5IGJ1aWxkaW5nLCBvciBldmVuIGxpdGVyYXR1cmUgcmV2aWV3cy0tIGFueS